NAME
       yield - give up the processor

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sched.h>

       int sched_yield(void);

DESCRIPTION
       Offers the rest of the current time slice to another runnable
       task of the same priority. The scheduler picks the next task
       from a priority bitmap, so the choice costs the same regardless
       of how many tasks exist.

       Yielding in a loop is a poor way to wait: use poll(2) with a
       timeout, or sleep, so the task is not runnable while it waits.

RETURN VALUE
       0.

SEE ALSO
       poll(2), clock(2), futex(2)
